§ `Section 19(1) -- the paragraphs`

-- (1.1): separated, and not solely because a partner is incarcerated: they have become former common-law partners.
#ASSERT `s 19(1.1): the common-law partners have become former common-law partners` `test facts where the person is separated from the pensioner is TRUE`
#ASSERT NOT `s 19(1.1): the common-law partners have become former common-law partners` `test facts where the person is separated from the pensioner is TRUE; the sole reason for the separation is is TRUE`
#ASSERT NOT `s 19(1.1): the common-law partners have become former common-law partners` `test base facts`
-- (1)(a): not separated: met.
#ASSERT `s 19(1)(a): the spouse meets the separation condition` `test month` `test base facts`
-- Separated, commenced June 1, 2022: three months before September is June 1, so not more than three months before: met.
-- Commenced May 31, 2022: more than three months before: not met.
#ASSERT `s 19(1)(a): the spouse meets the separation condition` `test month` `test facts where the person is separated from the pensioner is TRUE; the day on which the separation commenced is JUST (YMD 2022 6 1)`
#ASSERT NOT `s 19(1)(a): the spouse meets the separation condition` `test month` `test facts where the person is separated from the pensioner is TRUE; the day on which the separation commenced is JUST (YMD 2022 5 31)`
-- Separated with no date of separation: not met.
#ASSERT NOT `s 19(1)(a): the spouse meets the separation condition` `test month` `test facts where the person is separated from the pensioner is TRUE`
-- Separation must commence after June 30, 1999: for August 1999, commenced July 1, 1999: met; June 30, 1999: not met.
#ASSERT `s 19(1)(a): the spouse meets the separation condition` (YMD 1999 8 1) `test facts where the person is separated from the pensioner is TRUE; the day on which the separation commenced is JUST (YMD 1999 7 1)`
#ASSERT NOT `s 19(1)(a): the spouse meets the separation condition` (YMD 1999 8 1) `test facts where the person is separated from the pensioner is TRUE; the day on which the separation commenced is JUST (YMD 1999 6 30)`
-- (1.2): the sole reason for the separation is that the pensioner is incarcerated: not considered separated, however long.
#ASSERT `s 19(1)(a): the spouse meets the separation condition` `test month` `test facts where the person is separated from the pensioner is TRUE; the sole reason for the separation is is TRUE; the day on which the separation commenced is JUST (YMD 2010 1 1)`
-- (1)(a.1): a former common-law partner who separated on July 15, 2022: met. One who is not separated: not met.
#ASSERT `s 19(1)(a.1): the former common-law partner meets the separation condition` `test month` `test facts where the person is separated from the pensioner is TRUE; the day on which the separation commenced is JUST (YMD 2022 7 15)`
#ASSERT NOT `s 19(1)(a.1): the former common-law partner meets the separation condition` `test month` `test base facts`
#ASSERT NOT `s 19(1)(a.1): the former common-law partner meets the separation condition` `test month` `test facts where the person is separated from the pensioner is TRUE; the day on which the separation commenced is JUST (YMD 2022 5 31)`
-- (1)(b), born March 15, 1960: February 29, 2020 is the day before March 1, 2020: age 59: not. March 31, 2020 (the day before
-- April 1): age 60: yes. February 28, 2025: age 64: yes. March 31, 2025: age 65: no.
#ASSERT NOT `s 19(1)(b): the person is at least sixty and under sixty-five` (YMD 2020 3 20) `test base facts`
#ASSERT `s 19(1)(b): the person is at least sixty and under sixty-five` (YMD 2020 4 1) `test base facts`
#ASSERT `s 19(1)(b): the person is at least sixty and under sixty-five` (YMD 2025 3 10) `test base facts`
#ASSERT NOT `s 19(1)(b): the person is at least sixty and under sixty-five` (YMD 2025 4 1) `test base facts`
-- Born on the 1st (April 1, 1960): attains 60 on April 1, 2020: payable from May 2020 (the month after), not April. Attains 65
-- on April 1, 2025: payable through April 2025, not May.
#ASSERT NOT `s 19(1)(b): the person is at least sixty and under sixty-five` (YMD 2020 4 15) `test facts where the person's date of birth is YMD 1960 4 1`
#ASSERT `s 19(1)(b): the person is at least sixty and under sixty-five` (YMD 2020 5 15) `test facts where the person's date of birth is YMD 1960 4 1`
